                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 86.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 295.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 21, 1870</date>. (Received October
                    18.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose you herewith a correspondence I have had with some
                    German citizens of the United States, in relation to the protection afforded
                    them by American passports, and which explains itself.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>



